    environment: "underground",
    visualDescription: "This creature is a 4-foot tall frog-like humanoid with large, bulbous eyes that constantly emits bright yellow beams of light. Its skin is mottled yellow, growing darker across its back. Its feet are webbed as are its claws.",
    description: "Blindheims dwell in underground caverns and sustain themselves on a diet of funguses, molds, and small rodents. An extra eyelid allows the blindheim to \"turn off\" its eyes when it is sleeping or resting. A dead blindheim's eyes are dull gold in color. Blindheims are 4 feet tall and weigh about 150 pounds. A blindheim attacks by first blinding a foe with its gaze and then rushing in to use its bite attack. It can turn its eyes on and off as it wishes, but always leaves them on during combat. If overmatched, a blindheim flees. Credit The Blindheim originally appeared in the First Edition Fiend Folio (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1981) and is used by permission. Copyright Notice Author Scott Greene, based on original material by Roger Musson.",
