    visualDescription: "This giant beetle has a greenish-gray carapace and wing-covers, and its legs and mandibles are black.",
    description: "Boring beetles feed primarily on wood, mold, fungus, and other organic matter. They make their lairs inside ancient tunnels and caverns, where they harvest and grow molds and fungi. Shriekers are prized for both food and their use as alarms to warn the boring beetles of intrusion. Boring beetles are about 9 feet long. Boring beetles bite with their powerful mandibles. Slain victims are dragged to their lair and used to grow new molds and fungi. Credit The Boring Beetle originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1977) and is used by permission. Copyright Notice Author Scott Greene, based on original material by Gary Gygax.",
