    visualDescription: "This construct is a tangled mess of knotted and bundled ropes in roughly humanoid form.",
    description: "Rope golems are constructed from many intertwined and knotted ropes and often serve as guardians to lesser nobles, wizards, clerics, and the like, protecting a treasure hoard or some ancient knowledge best kept hidden. The typical rope golem stands 7 feet tall but weighs only about 100 pounds or so. Its long, gangly arms end in noose-like hands. A rope golem can expand its shape to fill a 10-foot area or contract its form to fill a space less than 2 1/2 feet square. Until it is activated, a rope golem appears to be nothing more than a pile of normal ropes. Rope golems cannot communicate. Rope golems attack by rolling their ropey appendages into \"fists\" and pummeling a foe. If a rope golem hits, it attempts to slip its noose-like hands over its opponent's head and around its neck. If successful, a rope golem often maintains the hold until it is destroyed or its opponent is dead. Construction A rope golem's body is spun and tied from 200 pounds of rope. Special bindings and powders worth 200 gp are used in the process. ROPE GOLEM CL 8th; Price 14,200 Requirements Craft Construct, animate rope, geas/quest, rope trick, creator must be caster level 8th; Skill Craft (ropemaking) DC 13; Cost 7,200 Copyright Notice Author Scott Greene.",
