    visualDescription: "This small dwarf-sized bipedal lizard has mottled gray and brown flesh with a short dorsal fin that runs the length of its body, tapering off as it meets the tail. Its underbelly is yellow and its eyes are white. Its feet are webbed as are its tiny \"hands.",
    description: "The muckdweller is a small, swamp-dwelling bipedal lizard that lives on a diet of carrion, fresh meat, plants, and insects. It has a long tail that allows it to swim rapidly through the water or maintain its balance when standing upright. Muckdwellers sometimes associate with lizardfolk. Muckdwellers stand about 4 feet tall. They speak their own language of croaks and hisses, and a rare few speak Draconic. The muckdweller attacks by squirting muddy water at its foes. When it successfully blinds an opponent, it darts in and bites with its sharp teeth. Credit The Muckdweller originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission. Copyright Notice Author Scott Greene, based on original material by Gary Gygax.",
