    visualDescription: "This creature resembles a rooster with thinning feathers and leathery bat-like wings lightly covered in reddish-tinged feathers. Its tail feathers are a yellowish-brown save for one bright red feather.",
    description: "The pyrolisk resembles a cockatrice and is often mistaken for it (Spot check at DC 25 to identify the pyrolisk successfully). The difference lies in the coloration of its tail feathers and wings: the pyrolisk has a single red feather in its tail and a reddish tinge to its wings. Otherwise, it is identical to the cockatrice in appearance. The pyrolisk uses its gaze attack to ignite those that are unaffected by the blinding flash of its pyrotechnic ability. It is a fierce combatant, fighting until either it or its opponents are dead. Credit The Pyrolisk originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission. Copyright Notice Author Scott Greene, based on original material by Gary Gygax.",
