        type: "Su",
        text: "As a standard action, a baba yaga can place a hex on any living creature within 60 feet. If the creature fails a DC 22 Fortitude save it takes 3d6 points of damage plus 2d6 bleed damage. A creature that fails its save by 5 or more also takes 1d2 points of Constitution damage. The bleeding can be stopped with a DC 15 Heal check or through the application of any magical healing. The save DC is Intelligence-based. Spells A baba yaga casts spells as a 12th-level witch (Pathfinder Roleplaying Game Advanced Player's Guide). They do not gain access to any other witch abilities.",
